# Track J regression net — `Guard[String].get()` used to double-free when the
# inner was a heap-carrying String: the runtime `.get()` returned a `void*` the
# compiler was treating as an OWNED T, so the caller local received a shallow
# copy of the Str header aliasing the Mutex-owned buffer. Scope-exit dropped
# both slots → `free(): double free detected in tcache 2` (exit 134).
#
# Post-fix: `Guard/ReadGuard/WriteGuard.get()` route at IR-lowering through
# `emit_guard_get_ptr` (the same helper the write path uses). The loaded value
# is tagged `LocalOwnership::View`, so drop-insertion emits no drop for it, and
# `ensure_owned_at_boundary` clones-if-borrow when the value flows into an
# owned position (return/ctor field/collection put).
#
# HEAP-FORCED VALUE (never a literal — a literal is a false negative per the
# durable-known_gaps rule; a rodata String has cap=0 so `gorget_string_free`
# short-circuits and the pre-fix compiler would appear clean).
String heaped():
    return "hello " + "world" + "-forced"

void main():
    Mutex[String] m = Mutex[String](heaped())
    Guard[String] g = m.lock()
    print(g.get())
